      "writtenOn": "2023-11-29T14:23:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "No, the pvmfw entry is a common part. What I mean is that the chain must always contain a minimum of three `DiceChainEntry` or `DiceChainEntryPayload` elements when we reach this point after the validation. In the `verify_dice_chain_up_to_pvmfw_payload` function, we have already checked the following:\n\n- service_vm_dice_chain.len() \u003e\u003d 3\n- client_vm_dice_chain.len() \u003d\u003d service_vm_dice_chain.len() - 1 + 2\n\nThis means client_vm_dice_chain.len() \u003e\u003d 4, while at the 0\u0027s index, we have the root key rather that a `DiceChainEntry`, we should have payloads.len() \u003e\u003d 3 here. This assertion is included here solely to enhance code clarity and to ensure that we can confidently access the last two items in payloads later on.",
      "parentUuid": "df857691_d6a30537",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 73,
        "startChar": 74,
        "endLine": 73,
        "endChar": 95
